{"id":"mahabharata-7-085","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":85,"title":"पञ्चाशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 85 · Satyaki against Drona","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks how Satyaki stood against Drona, and Sanjaya describes how Drona, greatly wrathful, killed Somakas and Panchalas. Satyaki fights back, and Yudhishthira, hearing the roar of Krishna's conch far off, grows anxious for Arjuna.","kn":"ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ದ್ರೋಣನನ್ನು ಹೇಗೆ ಎದುರಿಸಿದನೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸಂಜಯ ದ್ರೋಣ ಸೋಮಕ, ಪಾಂಚಾಲರನ್ನು ಕೊಂದದ್ದನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ತಿರುಗಿ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದೂರದಲ್ಲಿ ಕೃಷ್ಣನ ಶಂಖನಾದ ಕೇಳಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗಾಗಿ ಆತಂಕಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि सात्यकि द्रोण के सामने कैसे टिका, और संजय बताते हैं कि द्रोण ने क्रोध में सोमकों और पाञ्चालों को मारा। सात्यकि लड़ता है, और दूर कृष्ण के शंख की ध्वनि सुनकर युधिष्ठिर अर्जुन के लिए चिन्तित होते हैं।","te":"సాత్యకి ద్రోణుని ఎలా ఎదుర్కొన్నాడని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు; ద్రోణుడు కోపంతో సోమకులను, పాంచాలులను చంపిన తీరును సంజయుడు చెబుతాడు. సాత్యకి ఎదురు పోరాడతాడు; దూరంగా కృష్ణుని శంఖధ్వని విని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అర్జునుని గురించి కలవరపడతాడు.","ta":"சாத்யகி த்ரோணரை எவ்வாறு எதிர்த்தான் என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்க, த்ரோணர் சினத்துடன் சோமகரையும் பாஞ்சாலரையும் கொன்றதைச் சஞ்சயன் கூறுகிறான். சாத்யகி எதிர்த்துப் போரிட, தொலைவில் கண்ணனின் சங்கொலி கேட்டு யுதிஷ்டிரர் அர்ஜுனனுக்காகக் கவலைப்படுகிறார்.","ml":"സാത്യകി ദ്രോണരെ എങ്ങനെ നേരിട്ടുവെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; അത്യന്തം കോപിച്ച ദ്രോണർ സോമകരെയും പാഞ്ചാലരെയും വധിച്ചതായി സഞ്ജയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. സാത്യകി തിരിച്ചടിക്കുന്നു; ദൂരെനിന്ന് കൃഷ്ണന്റെ ശംഖനാദം കേട്ട യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ അർജുനനെക്കുറിച്ച് ഉത്കണ്ഠപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.85; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भारद्वाजं कथं युद्धे युयुधानोऽभ्यवारयत् ।\nसंजयाचक्ष्व तत्त्वेन परं कौतूहलं हि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, tell me truly how Yuyudhana held back Drona, the son of Bharadvaja, in the battle; my curiosity is very great."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"शृणु राजन्महाप्राज्ञ संग्रामं लोमहर्षणम् ।\nद्रोणस्य पाण्डवैः सार्धं युयुधानपुरोगमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen, O king of great wisdom, to the hair-raising battle between Drona and the Pandavas led by Yuyudhana."}},{"n":3,"text":"वध्यमानं बलं दृष्ट्वा युयुधानेन मारिष ।\nअभ्यद्रवत्स्वयं द्रोणः सात्यकिं सत्यविक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his army being cut down by Yuyudhana, O lord, Drona himself rushed at Satyaki, whose valor never fails."}},{"n":4,"text":"तमापतन्तं सहसा भारद्वाजं महारथम् ।\nसात्यकिः पञ्चविंशत्या क्षुद्रकाणां समार्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the great chariot-warrior Bharadvaja's son charged suddenly, Satyaki sent twenty-five kshudraka arrows into him."}},{"n":5,"text":"द्रोणोऽपि युधि विक्रान्तो युयुधानं समाहितः ।\nअविध्यत्पञ्चभिस्तूर्णं हेमपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona too, valiant in battle, steady, quickly pierced Yuyudhana with five stone-sharpened arrows with golden feathers."}},{"n":6,"text":"ते वर्म भित्त्वा सुदृढं द्विषत्पिशितभोजनाः ।\nअभ्यगुर्धरणीं राजञ्श्वसन्त इव पन्नगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those arrows, which feed on the flesh of enemies, broke through his strong armor and sank into the earth, O king, hissing like snakes."}},{"n":7,"text":"दीर्घबाहुरभिक्रुद्धस्तोत्त्रार्दित इव द्विपः ।\nद्रोणं पञ्चाशताविध्यन्नाराचैरग्निसंनिभैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The long-armed Satyaki, enraged like an elephant goaded with a hook, struck Drona with fifty fiery iron arrows."}},{"n":8,"text":"भारद्वाजो रणे विद्धो युयुधानेन सत्वरम् ।\nसात्यकिं बहुभिर्बाणैर्यतमानमविध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck quickly by Yuyudhana in battle, Bharadvaja's son pierced Satyaki, who was struggling hard, with many arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो महेष्वासो भूय एव महाबलः ।\nसात्वतं पीडयामास शतेन नतपर्वणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that mighty bowman, of great strength, angered again, tormented the Satvata with a hundred straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":10,"text":"स वध्यमानः समरे भारद्वाजेन सात्यकिः ।\nनाभ्यपद्यत कर्तव्यं किंचिदेव विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Being struck thus in battle by Bharadvaja's son, Satyaki, O lord of men, found no remedy at all."}},{"n":11,"text":"विषण्णवदनश्चापि युयुधानोऽभवन्नृप ।\nभारद्वाजं रणे दृष्ट्वा विसृजन्तं शिताञ्शरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yuyudhana's face fell, O king, when he saw Bharadvaja's son loosing sharp arrows in the fight."}},{"n":12,"text":"तं तु संप्रेक्ष्य ते पुत्राः सैनिकाश्च विशां पते ।\nप्रहृष्टमनसो भूत्वा सिंहवद्व्यनदन्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that, your sons and soldiers, O lord of men, grew glad at heart and roared again and again like lions."}},{"n":13,"text":"तं श्रुत्वा निनदं घोरं पीड्यमानं च माधवम् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरोऽब्रवीद्राजन्सर्वसैन्यानि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that terrible roar and knowing that the Madhava was hard pressed, Yudhishthira spoke to all the armies, O king."}},{"n":14,"text":"एष वृष्णिवरो वीरः सात्यकिः सत्यकर्मकृत् ।\nग्रस्यते युधि वीरेण भानुमानिव राहुणा ।\nअभिद्रवत गच्छध्वं सात्यकिर्यत्र युध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That best of the Vrishnis, the hero Satyaki, whose deeds are true, is being swallowed in battle by that hero, as Rahu swallows the sun. Rush there, go where Satyaki is fighting.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नं च पाञ्चाल्यमिदमाह जनाधिप ।\nअभिद्रव द्रुतं द्रोणं किं नु तिष्ठसि पार्षत ।\nन पश्यसि भयं घोरं द्रोणान्नः समुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He also said this to Dhrishtadyumna, the Panchala prince, O lord of men: \"Attack Drona quickly. Why do you stand there, son of Prishata? Do you not see the terrible danger that has come to us from Drona?"}},{"n":16,"text":"असौ द्रोणो महेष्वासो युयुधानेन संयुगे ।\nक्रीडते सूत्रबद्धेन पक्षिणा बालको यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, the mighty bowman Drona is playing with Yuyudhana in battle, as a boy plays with a bird tied by a string."}},{"n":17,"text":"तत्रैव सर्वे गच्छन्तु भीमसेनमुखा रथाः ।\nत्वयैव सहिता यत्ता युयुधानरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let all the chariots led by Bhimasena go there, alert, together with you, toward Yuyudhana's chariot."}},{"n":18,"text":"पृष्ठतोऽनुगमिष्यामि त्वामहं सहसैनिकः ।\nसात्यकिं मोक्षयस्वाद्य यमदंष्ट्रान्तरं गतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will follow behind you with my soldiers. Free Satyaki today, who has fallen between the fangs of Death.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततो राजा सर्वसैन्येन पाण्डवः ।\nअभ्यद्रवद्रणे द्रोणं युयुधानस्य कारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, King Yudhishthira the Pandava charged at Drona in battle with his whole army, for Yuyudhana's sake."}},{"n":20,"text":"तत्रारावो महानासीद्द्रोणमेकं युयुत्सताम् ।\nपाण्डवानां च भद्रं ते सृञ्जयानां च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a great clamor arose, as the Pandavas and Srinjayas, all of them, wishing to fight, converged on Drona alone, may good fortune be yours."}},{"n":21,"text":"ते समेत्य नरव्याघ्रा भारद्वाजं महारथम् ।\nअभ्यवर्षञ्शरैस्तीक्ष्णैः कङ्कबर्हिणवाजितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those tigers among men gathered round the great chariot-warrior Bharadvaja's son and rained on him sharp arrows fletched with heron and peacock feathers."}},{"n":22,"text":"स्मयन्नेव तु तान्वीरान्द्रोणः प्रत्यग्रहीत्स्वयम् ।\nअतिथीनागतान्यद्वत्सलिलेनासनेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona himself received those heroes, smiling, as one welcomes guests who have come, with water and a seat."}},{"n":23,"text":"तर्पितास्ते शरैस्तस्य भारद्वाजस्य धन्विनः ।\nआतिथेयगृहं प्राप्य नृपतेऽतिथयो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those bowmen were satisfied by the arrows of Bharadvaja's son, as guests are when they reach a host's house, O king."}},{"n":24,"text":"भारद्वाजं च ते सर्वे न शेकुः प्रतिवीक्षितुम् ।\nमध्यंदिनमनुप्राप्तं सहस्रांशुमिव प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"None of them could look at Bharadvaja's son, O lord, as one cannot look at the thousand-rayed sun when it reaches midday."}},{"n":25,"text":"तांस्तु सर्वान्महेष्वासान्द्रोणः शस्त्रभृतां वरः ।\nअतापयच्छरव्रातैर्गभस्तिभिरिवांशुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, best of weapon-bearers, scorched all those mighty bowmen with swarms of arrows, as the sun scorches with its rays."}},{"n":26,"text":"वध्यमाना रणे राजन्पाण्डवाः सृञ्जयास्तथा ।\nत्रातारं नाध्यगच्छन्त पङ्कमग्ना इव द्विपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck in the battle, O king, the Pandavas and Srinjayas found no protector, like elephants sunk in mud."}},{"n":27,"text":"द्रोणस्य च व्यदृश्यन्त विसर्पन्तो महाशराः ।\nगभस्तय इवार्कस्य प्रतपन्तः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona's great arrows were seen darting about, blazing on every side like the sun's rays."}},{"n":28,"text":"तस्मिन्द्रोणेन निहताः पाञ्चालाः पञ्चविंशतिः ।\nमहारथसमाख्याता धृष्टद्युम्नस्य संमताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Drona killed twenty-five Panchalas, famed as great chariot-warriors and esteemed by Dhrishtadyumna."}},{"n":29,"text":"पाण्डूनां सर्वसैन्येषु पाञ्चालानां तथैव च ।\nद्रोणं स्म ददृशुः शूरं विनिघ्नन्तं वरान्वरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In all the armies of the Pandus and the Panchalas, they saw the hero Drona cutting down the best of them one after another."}},{"n":30,"text":"केकयानां शतं हत्वा विद्राव्य च समन्ततः ।\nद्रोणस्तस्थौ महाराज व्यादितास्य इवान्तकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having slain a hundred Kekayas and scattered them everywhere, Drona stood, O great king, like Death with gaping mouth."}},{"n":31,"text":"पाञ्चालान्सृञ्जयान्मत्स्यान्केकयान्पाण्डवानपि ।\nद्रोणोऽजयन्महाबाहुः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty-armed Drona defeated the Panchalas, Srinjayas, Matsyas, Kekayas and Pandavas by hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":32,"text":"तेषां समभवच्छब्दो वध्यतां द्रोणसायकैः ।\nवनौकसामिवारण्ये दह्यतां धूमकेतुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"A cry rose from them as they were cut down by Drona's arrows, like the cry of forest creatures burned in the wood by fire."}},{"n":33,"text":"तत्र देवाः सगन्धर्वाः पितरश्चाब्रुवन्नृप ।\nएते द्रवन्ति पाञ्चालाः पाण्डवाश्च ससैनिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, O king, gods, Gandharvas and ancestors said, \"Look, the Panchalas and the Pandavas with their soldiers are fleeing.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"तं तथा समरे द्रोणं निघ्नन्तं सोमकान्रणे ।\nन चाप्यभिययुः केचिदपरे नैव विव्यधुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Drona thus slew the Somakas in battle, some did not approach him, and others did not shoot at him."}},{"n":35,"text":"वर्तमाने तथा रौद्रे तस्मिन्वीरवरक्षये ।\nअशृणोत्सहसा पार्थः पाञ्चजन्यस्य निस्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that dreadful slaughter of the best of heroes went on, Arjuna suddenly heard the sound of the Panchajanya."}},{"n":36,"text":"पूरितो वासुदेवेन शङ्खराट्स्वनते भृशम् ।\nयुध्यमानेषु वीरेषु सैन्धवस्याभिरक्षिषु ।\nनदत्सु धार्तराष्ट्रेषु विजयस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Filled by Vasudeva's breath, that king of conches sounded loudly, as the heroes guarding Saindhava fought and the Dhartarashtras roared toward Vijaya's chariot."}},{"n":37,"text":"गाण्डीवस्य च निर्घोषे विप्रनष्टे समन्ततः ।\nकश्मलाभिहतो राजा चिन्तयामास पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the sound of the Gandiva was lost everywhere, King Yudhishthira the Pandava, struck by dizziness, began to think."}},{"n":38,"text":"न नूनं स्वस्ति पार्थस्य यथा नदति शङ्खराट् ।\nकौरवाश्च यथा हृष्टा विनदन्ति मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely all is not well with Partha, since the king of conches sounds so, and the Kauravas shout again and again in joy.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"एवं संचिन्तयित्वा तु व्याकुलेनान्तरात्मना ।\nअजातशत्रुः कौन्तेयः सात्वतं प्रत्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking thus, with a troubled heart, Kunti's son Ajatashatru spoke to the Satvata."}},{"n":40,"text":"बाष्पगद्गदया वाचा मुह्यमानो मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nकृत्यस्यानन्तरापेक्षी शैनेयं शिनिपुंगवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His voice choking with tears, bewildered again and again, he turned to Shaineya, the bull of the Shinis, looking to what must be done next."}},{"n":41,"text":"यः स धर्मः पुरा दृष्टः सद्भिः शैनेय शाश्वतः ।\nसांपराये सुहृत्कृत्ये तस्य कालोऽयमागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Shaineya, the eternal duty that good men saw long ago, to serve a friend in battle, its time has now come."}},{"n":42,"text":"सर्वेष्वपि च योधेषु चिन्तयञ्शिनिपुंगव ।\nत्वत्तः सुहृत्तमं कंचिन्नाभिजानामि सात्यके ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking over all the warriors, bull of the Shinis, I know none who is a better friend to me than you, Satyaki."}},{"n":43,"text":"यो हि प्रीतमना नित्यं यश्च नित्यमनुव्रतः ।\nस कार्ये सांपराये तु नियोज्य इति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is always glad at heart and always devoted should, I believe, be assigned a task in a great battle."}},{"n":44,"text":"यथा च केशवो नित्यं पाण्डवानां परायणम् ।\nतथा त्वमपि वार्ष्णेय कृष्णतुल्यपराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Keshava is always the refuge of the Pandavas, so are you too, Vrishni, equal to Krishna in valor."}},{"n":45,"text":"सोऽहं भारं समाधास्ये त्वयि तं वोढुमर्हसि ।\nअभिप्रायं च मे नित्यं न वृथा कर्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will lay a burden on you, and you should bear it. You should never make my purpose in vain."}},{"n":46,"text":"स त्वं भ्रातुर्वयस्यस्य गुरोरपि च संयुगे ।\nकुरु कृच्छ्रे सहायार्थमर्जुनस्य नरर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, bull among men, in this hard time help Arjuna in battle, your brother, friend and teacher."}},{"n":47,"text":"त्वं हि सत्यव्रतः शूरो मित्राणामभयंकरः ।\nलोके विख्यायसे वीर कर्मभिः सत्यवागिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For you, hero, are firm in your vows, brave, and a giver of fearlessness to friends, known in the world for your deeds as one true to his word."}},{"n":48,"text":"यो हि शैनेय मित्रार्थे युध्यमानस्त्यजेत्तनुम् ।\nपृथिवीं वा द्विजातिभ्यो यो दद्यात्सममेव तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaineya, one who gives up his body fighting for a friend is like one who gives the earth to brahmins."}},{"n":49,"text":"श्रुताश्च बहवोऽस्माभी राजानो ये दिवं गताः ।\nदत्त्वेमां पृथिवीं कृत्स्नां ब्राह्मणेभ्यो यथाविधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have heard of many kings who went to heaven after duly giving this whole earth to brahmins."}},{"n":50,"text":"एवं त्वामपि धर्मात्मन्प्रयाचेऽहं कृताञ्जलिः ।\nपृथिवीदानतुल्यं स्यादधिकं वा फलं विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I, with joined palms, beg you too, righteous one: the fruit would be equal to the gift of the earth, or greater, my lord."}},{"n":51,"text":"एक एव सदा कृष्णो मित्राणामभयंकरः ।\nरणे संत्यजति प्राणान्द्वितीयस्त्वं च सात्यके ॥","meaning":{"en":"Only Krishna always gives fearlessness to friends and gives up his life in battle, and you are the second, Satyaki."}},{"n":52,"text":"विक्रान्तस्य च वीरस्य युद्धे प्रार्थयतो यशः ।\nशूर एव सहायः स्यान्नेतरः प्राकृतो जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a valiant hero who seeks fame in battle, only a hero can be a helper, not any common man."}},{"n":53,"text":"ईदृशे तु परामर्दे वर्तमानस्य माधव ।\nत्वदन्यो हि रणे गोप्ता विजयस्य न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In such a crush, Madhava, there is no one but you who can protect Vijaya in the fight."}},{"n":54,"text":"श्लाघन्नेव हि कर्माणि शतशस्तव पाण्डवः ।\nमम संजनयन्हर्षं पुनः पुनरकीर्तयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna himself, praising your deeds by the hundred, has repeatedly told them to me, giving me joy."}},{"n":55,"text":"लघ्वस्त्रश्चित्रयोधी च तथा लघुपराक्रमः ।\nप्राज्ञः सर्वास्त्रविच्छूरो मुह्यते न च संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said: quick with weapons, a marvelous fighter, quick in valor, wise, skilled in every weapon, brave, and never confused in battle."}},{"n":56,"text":"महास्कन्धो महोरस्को महाबाहुर्महाधनुः ।\nमहाबलो महावीर्यः स महात्मा महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Broad-shouldered, broad-chested, long-armed, great-bowed, very strong, of great prowess, great-souled, a great chariot-warrior."}},{"n":57,"text":"शिष्यो मम सखा चैव प्रियोऽस्याहं प्रियश्च मे ।\nयुयुधानः सहायो मे प्रमथिष्यति कौरवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is my pupil and my friend; I am dear to him and he to me. With Yuyudhana as my helper I shall crush the Kauravas."}},{"n":58,"text":"अस्मदर्थं च राजेन्द्र संनह्येद्यदि केशवः ।\nरामो वाप्यनिरुद्धो वा प्रद्युम्नो वा महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king of kings, even if Keshava, Rama, Aniruddha, or the great chariot-warrior Pradyumna were to arm for us,"}},{"n":59,"text":"गदो वा सारणो वापि साम्बो वा सह वृष्णिभिः ।\nसहायार्थं महाराज संग्रामोत्तममूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or Gada, or Sarana, or Samba, with the Vrishnis, to help us at the head of the best of battles, great king,"}},{"n":60,"text":"तथाप्यहं नरव्याघ्रं शैनेयं सत्यविक्रमम् ।\nसाहाय्ये विनियोक्ष्यामि नास्ति मेऽन्यो हि तत्समः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Still I would appoint that tiger among men, Shaineya, whose valor is true, to the help, for there is no other equal to him."}},{"n":61,"text":"इति द्वैतवने तात मामुवाच धनंजयः ।\nपरोक्षं त्वद्गुणांस्तथ्यान्कथयन्नार्यसंसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"So Dhananjaya told me, dear friend, in the Dvaita forest, speaking of your true virtues in your absence before a noble assembly."}},{"n":62,"text":"तस्य त्वमेवं संकल्पं न वृथा कर्तुमर्हसि ।\nधनंजयस्य वार्ष्णेय मम भीमस्य चोभयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You should not make that purpose of his vain, Vrishni, either of Dhananjaya, or of me, or of Bhima."}},{"n":63,"text":"यच्चापि तीर्थानि चरन्नगच्छं द्वारकां प्रति ।\nतत्राहमपि ते भक्तिमर्जुनं प्रति दृष्टवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And when I went on pilgrimages and came to Dvaraka, I too saw your devotion to Arjuna there."}},{"n":64,"text":"न तत्सौहृदमन्येषु मया शैनेय लक्षितम् ।\nयथा त्वमस्मान्भजसे वर्तमानानुपप्लवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaineya, I have seen no such affection in others as you show us when we are in distress."}},{"n":65,"text":"सोऽभिजात्या च भक्त्या च सख्यस्याचार्यकस्य च ।\nसौहृदस्य च वीर्यस्य कुलीनत्वस्य माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, by your noble birth, your devotion, your friendship, your tutelage, your goodwill, your valor, and your family, Madhava,"}},{"n":66,"text":"सत्यस्य च महाबाहो अनुकम्पार्थमेव च ।\nअनुरूपं महेष्वास कर्म त्वं कर्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your truthfulness, great-armed one, and also out of compassion, you ought to do a deed worthy of you, mighty bowman."}},{"n":67,"text":"सुयोधनो हि सहसा गतो द्रोणेन दंशितः ।\nपूर्वमेव तु यातास्ते कौरवाणां महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, armored by Drona, has gone off suddenly, and the great chariot-warriors of the Kauravas went ahead earlier."}},{"n":68,"text":"सुमहान्निनदश्चैव श्रूयते विजयं प्रति ।\nस शैनेय जवेनात्र गन्तुमर्हसि माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"A very great roar is heard around Vijaya. Madhava Shaineya, you should go there with speed."}},{"n":69,"text":"भीमसेनो वयं चैव संयत्ताः सहसैनिकाः ।\nद्रोणमावारयिष्यामो यदि त्वां प्रति यास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena and I, with our soldiers, will stay alert and will hold Drona back if he comes after you."}},{"n":70,"text":"पश्य शैनेय सैन्यानि द्रवमाणानि संयुगे ।\nमहान्तं च रणे शब्दं दीर्यमाणां च भारतीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, Shaineya, the armies fleeing in battle, the great noise in the fight, and the Bharata host being torn apart."}},{"n":71,"text":"महामारुतवेगेन समुद्रमिव पर्वसु ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रबलं तात विक्षिप्तं सव्यसाचिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like the sea at the full moon under a great gale, Dhritarashtra's host has been scattered by Savyasachin."}},{"n":72,"text":"रथैर्विपरिधावद्भिर्मनुष्यैश्च हयैश्च ह ।\nसैन्यं रजःसमुद्धूतमेतत्संपरिवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"This army is whirling about, with chariots, men and horses running in all directions, raised in a cloud of dust."}},{"n":73,"text":"संवृतः सिन्धुसौवीरैर्नखरप्रासयोधिभिः ।\nअत्यन्तापचितैः शूरैः फल्गुनः परवीरहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by Sindhus and Sauviras, who fight with claws and spears, by heroes devoted to the last, Phalguna, slayer of enemy heroes, is hemmed in."}},{"n":74,"text":"नैतद्बलमसंवार्य शक्यो हन्तुं जयद्रथः ।\nएते हि सैन्धवस्यार्थे सर्वे संत्यक्तजीविताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jayadratha cannot be killed without breaking through this force; all these have given up their lives for Saindhava."}},{"n":75,"text":"शरशक्तिध्वजवनं हयनागसमाकुलम् ।\nपश्यैतद्धार्तराष्ट्राणामनीकं सुदुरासदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at that Dhartarashtra host, so hard to reach, a forest of arrows, spears and banners, thick with horses and elephants."}},{"n":76,"text":"शृणु दुन्दुभिनिर्घोषं शङ्खशब्दांश्च पुष्कलान् ।\nसिंहनादरवांश्चैव रथनेमिस्वनांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear the booming of drums, the many conches, the lion-roars, and the rumble of chariot wheels."}},{"n":77,"text":"नागानां शृणु शब्दं च पत्तीनां च सहस्रशः ।\nसादिनां द्रवतां चैव शृणु कम्पयतां महीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear the trumpeting of elephants, the thousands of foot soldiers, and the cavalry, which shake the earth as they run."}},{"n":78,"text":"पुरस्तात्सैन्धवानीकं द्रोणानीकस्य पृष्ठतः ।\nबहुत्वाद्धि नरव्याघ्र देवेन्द्रमपि पीडयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In front is Saindhava's force, behind Drona's. Because of its numbers, tiger among men, it could press even Indra, lord of the gods."}},{"n":79,"text":"अपर्यन्ते बले मग्नो जह्यादपि च जीवितम् ।\nतस्मिंश्च निहते युद्धे कथं जीवेत मादृशः ।\nसर्वथाहमनुप्राप्तः सुकृच्छ्रं बत जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One sunk in a boundless army might even lose his life. And if he were killed in this battle, how could one like me live? Alas, I have in every way come to a very hard life."}},{"n":80,"text":"श्यामो युवा गुडाकेशो दर्शनीयश्च पाण्डवः ।\nलघ्वस्त्रश्चित्रयोधी च प्रविष्टस्तात भारतीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The dark young Gudakesha, the handsome Pandava, quick with weapons, a marvelous fighter, has entered the Bharata host, dear friend."}},{"n":81,"text":"सूर्योदये महाबाहुर्दिवसश्चातिवर्तते ।\nतन्न जानामि वार्ष्णेय यदि जीवति वा न वा ।\nकुरूणां चापि तत्सैन्यं सागरप्रतिमं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sun has risen, and the day is far gone, mighty-armed one. I do not know, Vrishni, whether he lives or not, in that vast Kuru army like an ocean."}},{"n":82,"text":"एक एव च बीभत्सुः प्रविष्टस्तात भारतीम् ।\nअविषह्यां महाबाहुः सुरैरपि महामृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bibhatsu alone, dear friend, has entered the Bharata host, which even the gods could not bear in a great battle."}},{"n":83,"text":"न च मे वर्तते बुद्धिरद्य युद्धे कथंचन ।\nद्रोणोऽपि रभसो युद्धे मम पीडयते बलम् ।\nप्रत्यक्षं ते महाबाहो यथासौ चरति द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My mind does not work at all in this battle today. And Drona too, furious in battle, is crushing my army, as you see with your own eyes, mighty-armed, as that brahmin ranges about."}},{"n":84,"text":"युगपच्च समेतानां कार्याणां त्वं विचक्षणः ।\nमहार्थं लघुसंयुक्तं कर्तुमर्हसि माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are wise when many tasks come together; you should do the one of great import that can be done quickly, Madhava."}},{"n":85,"text":"तस्य मे सर्वकार्येषु कार्यमेतन्मतं सदा ।\nअर्जुनस्य परित्राणं कर्तव्यमिति संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among all my tasks, this has always been my judgment: that Arjuna's protection must be secured in battle."}},{"n":86,"text":"नाहं शोचामि दाशार्हं गोप्तारं जगतः प्रभुम् ।\nस हि शक्तो रणे तात त्रीँल्लोकानपि संगतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not grieve for Dasharha, protector of the world, the lord. He is able, dear friend, to conquer even the three worlds together in battle, tiger among men; I tell you this truly."}},{"n":87,"text":"विजेतुं पुरुषव्याघ्र सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ।\nकिं पुनर्धार्तराष्ट्रस्य बलमेतत्सुदुर्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How much easier, then, to beat this very weak Dhartarashtra force."}},{"n":88,"text":"अर्जुनस्त्वेव वार्ष्णेय पीडितो बहुभिर्युधि ।\nप्रजह्यात्समरे प्राणांस्तस्माद्विन्दामि कश्मलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Arjuna, Vrishni, pressed by many in battle, might give up his life in the fight; that is why I feel faint."}},{"n":89,"text":"तस्य त्वं पदवीं गच्छ गच्छेयुस्त्वादृशा यथा ।\nतादृशस्येदृशे काले मादृशेनाभिचोदितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Follow his path, as men like you may follow; I, a man like me, urge you at such a time for such a man."}},{"n":90,"text":"रणे वृष्णिप्रवीराणां द्वावेवातिरथौ स्मृतौ ।\nप्रद्युम्नश्च महाबाहुस्त्वं च सात्वत विश्रुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the heroic Vrishnis in battle only two are remembered as atirathas: the mighty-armed Pradyumna and you, renowned Satvata."}},{"n":91,"text":"अस्त्रे नारायणसमः संकर्षणसमो बले ।\nवीरतायां नरव्याघ्र धनंजयसमो ह्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"In weapons you equal Narayana, in strength Sankarshana, and in heroism, tiger among men, you equal Dhananjaya."}},{"n":92,"text":"भीष्मद्रोणावतिक्रम्य सर्वयुद्धविशारदम् ।\nत्वामद्य पुरुषव्याघ्रं लोके सन्तः प्रचक्षते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Passing over Bhishma and Drona, the good in the world say today that you are the tiger among men skilled in all warfare."}},{"n":93,"text":"नासाध्यं विद्यते लोके सात्यकेरिति माधव ।\nतत्त्वां यदभिवक्ष्यामि तत्कुरुष्व महाबल ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nothing in the world is impossible for Satyaki, Madhava. So do what I will say to you, mighty one."}},{"n":94,"text":"संभावना हि लोकस्य तव पार्थस्य चोभयोः ।\nनान्यथा तां महाबाहो संप्रकर्तुमिहार्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the world's expectation rests on you and on Partha both; you should not make it otherwise, mighty-armed."}},{"n":95,"text":"परित्यज्य प्रियान्प्राणान्रणे विचर वीरवत् ।\nन हि शैनेय दाशार्हा रणे रक्षन्ति जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give up your dear life and range in battle like a hero. The Dasharhas, Shaineya, do not guard their lives in battle."}},{"n":96,"text":"अयुद्धमनवस्थानं संग्रामे च पलायनम् ।\nभीरूणामसतां मार्गो नैष दाशार्हसेवितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"To avoid fighting, to refuse to stand firm, to flee in battle, is the way of cowards and bad men; it is not followed by the Dasharhas."}},{"n":97,"text":"तवार्जुनो गुरुस्तात धर्मात्मा शिनिपुंगव ।\nवासुदेवो गुरुश्चापि तव पार्थस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna is your teacher, dear friend, the righteous one, bull of the Shinis, and Vasudeva is the teacher of the wise Partha."}},{"n":98,"text":"कारणद्वयमेतद्धि जानानस्त्वाहमब्रुवम् ।\nमावमंस्था वचो मह्यं गुरुस्तव गुरोर्ह्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing these two reasons I have spoken to you. Do not slight my words; I am the teacher of your teacher."}},{"n":99,"text":"वासुदेवमतं चैतन्मम चैवार्जुनस्य च ।\nसत्यमेतन्मयोक्तं ते याहि यत्र धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the wish of Vasudeva, of me, and of Arjuna. I have told you the truth: go where Dhananjaya is."}},{"n":100,"text":"एतद्वचनमाज्ञाय मम सत्यपराक्रम ।\nप्रविशैतद्बलं तात धार्तराष्ट्रस्य दुर्मतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing my words, you whose valor is true, enter the army of the evil-minded Dhartarashtra, dear friend."}},{"n":101,"text":"प्रविश्य च यथान्यायं संगम्य च महारथैः ।\nयथार्हमात्मनः कर्म रणे सात्वत दर्शय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having entered it as is fitting, and having met the great chariot-warriors, show your own deed in battle as it befits you, Satvata."}}]}]}